From trettel@fee.unicamp.br Fri Sep  5 10:46:01 1997
Message-ID: <199709051744.NAA08217@linux03.amt.tay1.dec.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 1997 15:45:46 -0300 (EST)
From: Eduardo A. Trettel <trettel@fee.unicamp.br>
Subject: Re: Installing aboot

On Thu, 4 Sep 1997 Stephen J. Gaudet write:

> What I would do is run fdisk, BSD label and look at what it thinks the 
> drive parameters should be. My guess is the counts you are using are
> possibly causing the problem. I haven't see a disk yet that ran under
> 62~63 sectors.
> This is where I believe the problem to be.
>
> What disk drive do you have?
>
> Regards,
>
> Steve

Hello Steve:
	The disk is a DEC RZ28D, 2007 MB, 4110480 sectors. The CHS values
given by bsdlabel are 2595/16/99. This values match those I found
factoring 4110480. Since fdisk doesnt allow you to set sectors higher than
63, I swaped the heads and sectors values, and divided the cylinders by 3
(just to keep it below 1024..), multiplying heads by the same values,
which gives 865/99/48 for CHS. This is the geometry I'm using. 

								Regards,
