Did you login with the same uid as when you tried it without strace?
My point just being that it is important who you login as, as the files being
run in the login process may differ and most importantly they may be
on a different filesystem and/or computer.

Another thing you might try is to run 'netstat -c -t' and check if the 
login socket hangs in the CLOSE_WAIT state even longer than they do
when I login. As I mentioned in another mail there is a bug/feature/something
that hangs the login socket in that state for three seconds on some Linux 
versions I run. Your version perhaps has an even longer timeout...

