Subject: How to get DEC OSF1 floating point behavior?

Hi,

I'm a happy Alpha Linux 4.2 user but I'd like to get "normal" Unix
behavior on floating point overflow. This statement:

	double a = 1.0/exp(720);

on OSF1, SunOS, and HP-UX quietly sets a to 0.0. On Linux is causes
an FPE trap, even if I set SIGFPE to SIG_IGN.

Any suggestions for how to get back to the old "silent" behavior?

Thanks,
Rick Woudenberg
-----------------------------------
My test program:

#include <signal.h>
double exp();

main()
{
    double e;

    printf("signal = %d\n", signal(SIGFPE, SIG_IGN));

    e = 1.0/exp(720.0);
    printf("e = %e\n", e);
}

